From: CoreNode homelab <noreply@corenode.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm53: admit native Next architecture to SM120 sparse MLA

SGLang's dedicated FlashInfer sparse-MLA guard predates GLM-5.3.  It accepts
the older GlmMoeDsa target and NextN architecture names, but rejects the native
Glm5Next target after the weights and draft have loaded.  GLM-5.3 uses the same
guarded GLM DSA contract: SM120/SM121, FP8 E4M3 KV, and the dedicated
flashinfer_sparse_mla backend for both prefill and decode.

Extend only the architecture allowlist.  All existing device, KV-dtype,
platform, and paired-backend checks remain fail closed.

---
 python/sglang/kernels/ops/attention/flash_mla_sm120.py | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/python/sglang/kernels/ops/attention/flash_mla_sm120.py b/python/sglang/kernels/ops/attention/flash_mla_sm120.py
--- a/python/sglang/kernels/ops/attention/flash_mla_sm120.py
+++ b/python/sglang/kernels/ops/attention/flash_mla_sm120.py
@@ -28,6 +28,8 @@
 _GLM_DSA_MODEL_ARCHS = (
     "GlmMoeDsaForCausalLM",
     "GlmMoeDsaForCausalLMNextN",
+    "Glm5NextForConditionalGeneration",
+    "Glm5NextForConditionalGenerationNextN",
 )
 
 # Page layout constants for DSv4-Flash (MODEL1):
